{"tier": "development", "anchor": null, "warmup": {"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one disk to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be restored quickly and accurately when a disaster occurs.\n\nHere is a detailed guide on designing a professional-grade file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Backup Strategies: Full vs. Incremental\nThe goal is to balance **data completeness** with **storage efficiency** and **backup speed**.\n\n#### Full Backups\nA full backup copies every selected file and folder, regardless of whether they have changed since the last backup.\n*   **Pros:** Sim", "elapsed_s": 3.666638207039796, "ttft_s": 0.5335830230033025, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 182, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 54, "prompt_ms": 471.669, "prompt_per_token_ms": 8.73461111111111, "prompt_per_second": 114.48706614172227, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3132.946, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.668866141732284, "predicted_per_second": 40.53692594765438}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 40.53551327378111, "end_to_end_output_tps": 34.90936186565809, "full_output_budget": true}, "measured": [{"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one drive to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be restored quickly and accurately when a disaster occurs.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive guide to designing a professional-grade file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Core Strategy: The 3-2-1 Rule\nBefore choosing tools, adhere to the industry standard for data protection:\n*   **3 Copies of Data:** Your primary data plus two backups.\n*   **2 Different Media Types:** (e.g., an internal SSD and an external USB", "elapsed_s": 3.6695094990427606, "ttft_s": 0.5333200240274891, "usage"